From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-ppe: declare ppe_drv_pppoe_alloc_secondary()

The helper is called from ppe_drv_pppoe_veip_l3_if_attach(), which this
configuration compiles out, so the function has no caller here but keeps
external linkage.  Mainline's -Wmissing-prototypes (6.10) rejects it and
making it static would only trade that for -Wunused-function.

Declare it next to ppe_drv_pppoe_alloc() in the header.  Declaration-only
change; the function stays available to the VEIP/PON builds that do call
it.
diff -ruN a/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_pppoe.h b/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_pppoe.h
--- a/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_pppoe.h
+++ b/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_pppoe.h
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 struct ppe_drv_pppoe *ppe_drv_pppoe_find_session_by_tl_l3_if(struct ppe_drv_tun_l3_if *tl_l3_if);
 struct ppe_drv_pppoe *ppe_drv_pppoe_find_session(uint16_t session_id, uint8_t *smac);
 struct ppe_drv_pppoe *ppe_drv_pppoe_alloc(uint16_t session_id, uint8_t *smac);
+struct ppe_drv_pppoe *ppe_drv_pppoe_alloc_secondary(uint16_t session_id, uint8_t *smac);
 
 void ppe_drv_pppoe_entries_free(struct ppe_drv_pppoe *pppoe);
 struct ppe_drv_pppoe *ppe_drv_pppoe_entries_alloc(void);
